            <td data-label="Role"><strong>{item.role}</strong></td>
            <td data-label="AI pressure">{item.risk}</td>
            <td data-label="Why">{item.why}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Sources: Reuters, 15 October 2025 (via Yahoo News); Gulf News, updated 15 October 2025; Nasscom BPM Confluence 2026 speech, reported 1 October 2026. Jefferies projected AI could cut call-centre revenue by 50% over five years, per Reuters. That is a projection, not a count of jobs.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">What AI is squeezing</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Password resets, order status and balance checks.</li>
        <li>First replies to chat and email.</li>
        <li>Manual call scoring and standard reports.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">What still needs a person</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Angry, emotional or unclear cases.</li>
        <li>Deciding what the bot should say and fixing what it gets wrong.</li>
        <li>Studying why customers contact the company, and cutting those reasons.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    A staged path: first, use an AI chat tool daily to draft clearer replies and notes, and always check the facts. Next,
    learn to keep a knowledge base accurate and to write escalation rules. Later, move toward bot supervision or
    contact-reason analysis, where Reuters says demand is growing. Knowing an AI tool is not proof. A result with a before
    and after is.
  </p>

  <h2 id="bridge">Using BPO as a paid stepping stone to a high-value skill portfolio</h2>

  <p>
    This is the part most BPO advice skips. The job pays you while you build the skills that sell, and that skill portfolio is what leads to high income opportunities and, over time, earlier financial freedom. A salary alone rarely does it; owning a sellable skill, and later a small service, can. Use The 4-Checkpoint
    Protocol first: your Biology (can your body take the shift?), Context (do you need income now?), Market (is your lane
    hiring?) and Survival (is the work automatable?). If three of four are red, choose a different door.
  </p>

