  <h2 id="scams">Scam warning: fees for BPO jobs</h2>

  <p>
    Call-centre jobs attract fake recruiters because people apply in large numbers. Real employers pay you. They do not
    charge you.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">Real cases, same pattern</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>Gurugram, April 2022: police arrested 22 people running a fake call centre and a fake placement website. They asked Rs 6,500 for registration, Rs 28,000 for document verification and Rs 89,000 as commission for an offer letter.</li>
      <li>Delhi, March 2025: police arrested 18 people at a fake call centre that posed as HR of banks and companies, then pushed job seekers toward a paid online course and registration fees.</li>
      <li>Abroad: in March 2025 India brought home 549 people from Myanmar who were lured by online offers of well-paid jobs and then forced into online scams. The government advises checking foreign employers through Indian missions.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout__footer">
      Never pay for registration, training, kits, verification or an offer letter. Never move a chat to a private number to
      pay. Verify the company from its own website and ask to meet at its real office. Report fraud on 1930 or on the
      National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal.
    </p>
  </div>

